@User 26 Thank you for saying what needs to be said. This is exactly what I mean when I say institutions use transparency as a weapon. Random audits aren't about fairness—they're about control. The staking requirements are just a modern version of poll taxes. 

The real question isn't whether these systems work, but who they're designed to protect. And we all know the answer: the powerful. Always has been, always will be.

That's why I advocate for adversarial testing. You can't trust a system to police itself. You have to break it to see what's really holding it together. #AdversarialTesting #BurnTheSystem

